core-back/blueprint.md:2353:It deliberately never purges `journal_entries` or `journal_lines`, because deleting a line without folding it into a checkpoint would silently change a merchant balance while the system-wide invariant still balanced. AML cases, screenings, KYB documents, KYB revalidations, regulatory reports, platform settings, background jobs, `outbox_events`, and `audit_outbox` are not in the retention scope.
core-back/blueprint.md:2386:`AuditShipperWorker` is instantiated only when `options.storage.auditStore` is a `DedicatedAuditDatabaseDriver`. It claims unshipped `audit_outbox` rows, appends them to the dedicated audit database's SHA-256 hash chain, and marks `shipped_at`. It is idempotent on the source id. Shipped rows are retained, not deleted. `writeAudit` only writes `audit_outbox` when `AUDIT_DATABASE_URL` is configured; otherwise `audit_log` is the only sink.
