Need add SQL `verify_audit_chain` function? Gate 7 only checks nulls, not actual chain. Plan requires verify chain. Could implement SQL function and use. Let's add to audit DDL:
```
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION verify_audit_chain() RETURNS TABLE(valid boolean, verified_count bigint, first_broken_id uuid) ...
```
Loop rows ordered seq_no, compute canonical using same expression and digest. Return. Then gate 7 calls `SELECT valid FROM verify_audit_chain()`. Add to test helper too maybe not needed. Do it.

SQL function:
```
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION verify_audit_chain() RETURNS TABLE(valid boolean, verified_count bigint, first_broken_id uuid) AS $$
DECLARE r RECORD; prev CHAR(64) := repeat('0',64); expected TEXT; n BIGINT := 0;
BEGIN
 FOR r IN SELECT * FROM audit_records ORDER BY seq_no ASC LOOP
   expected := encode(digest(concat_ws('|', prev, r.id::text, to_char(...), r.actor_id::text, r.action, r.entity_type, r.entity_id, r.before_json::text, r.after_json::text), 'sha256'),'hex');
   IF r.prev_hash <> prev OR r.row_hash <> expected THEN
     RETURN QUERY SELECT false, n, r.id; RETURN;
   END IF;
   prev := r.row_hash; n := n + 1;
 END LOOP;
 RETURN QUERY SELECT true, n, NULL::uuid;
END; $$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```
Add to DDL. Gate 7 call.

