`RailRoute` has no gatewayVersionId; it has gatewayId. The code selects gatewayVersionId incorrectly. This is hit by `listRouteInquirySupport` likely PollWorker. Fix: join gateway versions? `RailRoute` has gatewayId; GatewayVersion has gatewayId and maybe route-specific? The route doesn't pin version; current live version per gateway. For inquiry support, map gatewayId -> latest LIVE gatewayVersion setting. Simplest:
```
const routes = railRoute.findMany({select:{id:true,gatewayId:true}});
const settings = gatewaySetting.findMany({select:{gatewayVersionId:true,supportsStatusCheck:true}});
const versions = gatewayVersion.findMany({select:{id:true,gatewayId:true}});
map gatewayId -> versionId (latest? first) -> supports.
```
Need select latest. `gatewayVersion` has state. Could findMany where state LIVE. Implement. This is core bug. Patch.

